First you'll need to enter dependencies/ folder and type: make
That also fetches the prebuilt SWORD.xcframework
(iOS device and Apple silicon simulator, arm64, iOS 15.0) into
../cordova/cordova-plugin-crosswire-sword/libs/ios/

Then type make here to copy defs.h and flatapi.h into the plugin.

iOS needs no curl: HTTP(S) goes through Apple's NSURLSession
(src/mgr/nsurlhttpt.mm, NSURLAVAILABLE) and FTP through sword's ftplib,
so the app carries no TLS of its own.

To rebuild the xcframework: target SWORD of SWORD/SWORD.xcodeproj for
iphoneos and iphonesimulator, then xcodebuild -create-xcframework.  The
README beside each download in
crosswire.org/ftpmirror/pub/sword/dependencies/apple/ gives the details.
